The wind whipped Elsie's hair around her face as she gripped the rusty railing, her feet hanging over the edge of the precarious rooftop ledge. Below, rooftops tumbled away, a miniature version of the bustling city sprawling beneath her like a giant chessboard.  Elsie was used to this view, but tonight, it seemed even bigger, even more impressive.  Tonight, it felt like she was on the edge of the world.

“Ready?” whispered a voice from below, tinged with nervous excitement. 

